  "hypotheses": [
    "A signed, stable full-host publisher snapshot can be sealed into a launch authorization and revalidated across pre-open, post-open, pre-spawn validation, and final Popen preparation without accepting caller-supplied PCI identity or topology authority.",
    "An active sealed snapshot authorization, an active durable lease authorization, a fresh complete-group raw VFIO cdev/IOMMUFD capability, and an immutable fd-only render are sufficient for stock QEMU to perform its own IOMMUFD bind and IOAS attach without reparsing a host BDF.",
    "A paused QMP/QOM observation and successful VFIO/IOMMUFD ioctl trace are strong stock-QEMU component observations, but neither is an independent proof of DMA or interrupt isolation.",
    "Without a receipt from a DMA observer independent of the QMP observer, the launch transaction must never commit ATTACHED and must retain the complete lease claims in quarantine."
  ],
