  "limitations": [
    "This is one nested virtual e1000e in a one-member IOMMU group. It does not validate a multi-device group, a physical NIC/GPU/HBA, or a production compatibility profile.",
    "The syscall trace observes successful stock-QEMU bind/IOAS/attach calls in the same guest kernel; it does not independently prove DMA or interrupt-remapping isolation.",
    "The snapshot publisher and QMP observer use component HMAC keys. They are not a production trust root, TPM-backed signer, or key-rotation/revocation proof, and no independent DMA observer or receipt was available.",
    "The host-local SQLite authority has no external monotonic rollback anchor, so any earlier still-valid database state may be replayed, including same-key in-place/block restoration or deletion of the newest rows; inode and store UUID checks are not anti-rollback proof.",
    "Reset execution and verification, driver restoration, pidfd ownership, crash/power-loss recovery, DMA/IRQ teardown, multi-host fencing, and physical clean state were not proved.",
    "The bounded snapshot component does not implement the production qualification signer/catalog, host-agent/controller integration, kernel atomic topology generation, or physical-device qualification required by G1 and later milestones.",
